  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pilot digital skills development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Students from Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) institutes in Ethiopia, even after completing their education, generally lack basic or average levels of digital literacy and skills. This leaves them in a disadvantaged position on the job market.This pilot project addresses this issue by offering good quality tailor-made training-of-trainers (ToT) training on digital skills to a group of 100 TVET trainers. These trainers will then integrate these digital trainings into their regular curriculum and train an estimated group of 1,500 TVET students.If the training is successful and shows positive effects on entrepreneurship and employability, it could be scaled up and be offered at all TVETs in Addis Ababa with support of the larger Dutch-supported LIWAY (Livelihoods Improvement for Women and Youth) project.</narrative>
  </description>
